    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "A major power plant failure left the Visayas grid in crisis. When Kepco SPC Power's Unit 2 tripped offline, the Philippines grid operator declared a red alert. Officials then mandated emergency load shedding to prevent overloading a critical 230-kilovolt transmission line. This resulted in a huge loss of power for ordinary people, with more than 950 megawatts becoming unavailable—a stark capacity loss for the region.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Everyman",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-1",
          "how-2",
          "result-0"
        ],
        "center": "result-0",
        "center_kind": "result",
        "channel": "toned",
        "channel_role": "element_centered",
        "composition_mode": "ADR-0008",
        "salience_rank": 0
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.88
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "To stabilize the grid, authorities mandated power cuts across the Visayas. This emergency measure came after a power unit failed and seasonal heat drove demand into a thin operating margin. The grid management action was a direct response to high summer demand straining the system, forcing officials to order rolling blackouts to prevent a wider grid incident.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Everyman",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "why-2",
          "how-1",
          "how-2"
        ],
        "center": "how-2",
        "center_kind": "how",
        "channel": "toned",
        "channel_role": "element_centered",
        "composition_mode": "ADR-0008",
        "salience_rank": 1
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.82
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "From the view of a machine everyone depends on, the crisis was a collapse. The generating unit at Kepco SPC Power, a key piece of energy infrastructure, was the broken link in a chain already strained by ongoing shutdowns at other plants. Its failure triggered a cascade, forcing the grid into an emergency response that left hundreds of thousands of homes without power.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Everyman",
        "fragments": [
